  "heading_path": [
    "Trade Marks Regulations 1995",
    "Part 17A—Protected international trade marks under the Madrid Protocol",
    "Division 3—International registration designating Australia",
    "Subdivision 1—General",
    "17A.24  Final decision on examination"
  ],
  "instrument": "TMR1995",
  "kind": "regulation",
  "number": "17A.24",
  "ref": "TMR1995/r17A.24",
  "text": "(1) The Registrar must, after the examination, accept the IRDA unless he or she is satisfied that: (a) it is not in accordance with this Division; or (b) there are grounds for rejecting it. Note: Regulation 17A.28 sets out the grounds for rejecting an IRDA. (2) The Registrar may accept the IRDA subject to conditions or limitations. (3) The Registrar must reject an IRDA, in whole or in part, if the Registrar is satisfied that: (a) it is not in accordance with this Division; or (b) there are grounds for rejecting it, in whole or in part. Note: Regulation 17A.28 sets out the grounds for rejecting an IRDA.",
  "title": "Final decision on examination",
